.Dd $Mdocdate: May 16 2026 $
.Dt MAPED 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm maped
.Nd configure MAP-E Customer Edge state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 1dfp
.Op Fl i Ar seconds
.Op Fl l Ar level
.Op Ar config
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
monitors DHCPv6 MAP-E lease state and configures the local Customer Edge
runtime.
When lease data changes, or when the configured runtime state differs,
.Nm
runs
.Pa /usr/local/libexec/maped/maped-up
to configure the
.Xr gif 4
interface,
.Xr pf 4
anchor, and IPv4 default route.
Shared IPv4 allocations emit
.Cm map-e-portset
NAT rules, while unshared 1:1 IPv4 allocations
.Pq Va PSID_LEN Cm 0
emit unrestricted
.Cm nat-to
rules.
.Pp
The helper programs are installed under
.Pa /usr/local/libexec/maped
and are not intended to be run directly.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl 1
Run once and exit non-zero if provisioning or configuration fails.
.It Fl d
Daemonize.
.It Fl f
Run in the foreground and log to standard output.
.It Fl i Ar seconds
Set the polling or health-check interval.
The default is 30 seconds.
.It Fl l Ar level
Set the logging level.
Valid levels are
.Cm debug ,
.Cm info ,
and
.Cm warn .
The default is
.Cm info .
.It Fl p
Accepted for backward compatibility;
.Nm
always uses base Perl without external event packages.
.El
.Pp
If
.Ar config
is not specified,
.Nm
reads
.Pa /etc/maped.conf .
.Pp
External commands are limited to 30 seconds and 1 MiB of captured output.
Timed-out helper process groups are terminated.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The daemon and helpers accept the same literal shell-style assignments.
Values may be unquoted, single-quoted, or double-quoted.
Comments outside quotes are supported.
Variable expansion, command substitution, escapes, and shell commands
are rejected; use explicit values instead.
Restart the daemon after editing the configuration.
It passes a frozen, safely quoted configuration to each helper,
so an edit cannot change only half of an operation.
The following variables can be set:
.Bl -tag -width MAPED_PUBLISH_FILE
.It Va WAN_IF
IPv6 WAN interface.
.It Va LEASE_IF
Interface passed to
.Xr dhcp6leasectl 8 .
.It Va LAN_NET
IPv4 LAN network or table expression used in generated
.Xr pf 4
rules.
.It Va GIF_IF
.Xr gif 4
interface to create.
.It Va GIF_MTU
MTU assigned to
.Va GIF_IF .
The default,
.Cm auto ,
uses the current
.Va WAN_IF
MTU minus the 40-byte IPv6 encapsulation header each time the helper runs.
The route to the border relay must use that WAN interface.
A numeric value overrides automatic selection.
The result must be in the
.Xr gif 4
range 1280 through 8192; otherwise the helper fails before changing interfaces.
The generated anchor clamps IPv4 TCP MSS to this MTU minus 40.
For a PPPoE MTU of 1492, these values are 1452 and 1412, respectively.
This is initial interface sizing, not tunnel path MTU discovery.
Health checks recompute it when the WAN MTU changes.
This does not discover smaller downstream links.
Use a lower explicit MTU when the path requires it.
.It Va LEASE_FILE
Optional lease file used only as a change notification trigger.
Persisted lease contents do not authorize service.
The daemon queries current
.Xr dhcp6leasectl 8
state with
.Fl l Fl m
and requires an exact remaining lifetime.
Install the matching patched control utility before upgrading
.Nm .
.It Va PF_ANCHOR_FILE
Path used to store the generated
.Xr pf 4
anchor.
.It Va MAPED_PUBLISH_FILE
Optional JSON service file, read at startup.
Publishing is disabled when unset.
Restart
.Nm
after editing this file.
.It Va MAPED_UP
Runtime configuration helper.
.It Va MAPED_DOWN
Ownership-aware withdrawal helper.
.It Va MAPED_DERIVE
Optional override for the MAP-E parameter derivation helper.
When unset or set to the default helper path,
.Nm
derives parameters directly in-process and passes the derived values to
.Pa maped-up
without spawning a separate derivation process.
.It Va MAPED_STATE_DIR
Directory used for daemon state.
.It Va MAPED_MAX_HISTORY
Optional positive integer bounding the number of entries retained in the
.Cm record
and
.Cm publish_events
arrays in
.Pa status.json .
When unset, all observed transitions are retained.
.It Va MAPED_PEER_IPV4
Peer address used on the
.Xr gif 4
interface.
.It Va MAPED_LOG_LEVEL
Logging level for
.Nm .
.El
.Pp
Confirmed withdrawal or expiry removes the owned MAP-E configuration.
A temporary control-query failure retains service only until the last
confirmed monotonic deadline.
After restart, a failed query retires previously recorded ownership because
there is no in-memory proof that the old lease remains valid.
The state directory must be owned by
.Li root
and not writable by group or other.
Only one daemon may own it at a time.
Reserve the configured
.Xr gif 4
interface and the
.Dq mape
.Xr pf 4
anchor for this daemon.
Cleanup deletes the default route only when it still belongs to the recorded
tunnel, and removes the CE alias only when
.Nm
originally added it.
Legacy
.Pa lease.state
files alone are not ownership records.
.Sh INBOUND PUBLISHING
The optional publishing JSON object contains a
.Cm services
array.
Each entry requires a unique
.Cm name ,
a
.Cm protocol
of
.Cm tcp
or
.Cm udp ,
a
.Cm target_address
of
.Li 127.0.0.1 ,
and a
.Cm target_port
from 1 through 65535.
An optional
.Cm source_table
names an administrator-managed
.Xr pf 4
table without angle brackets.
Without a table, the rule permits any source.
Names start with a letter and contain at most 48 letters, digits, underscores,
or hyphens; table names contain at most 31 letters, digits, or underscores and
must not start with a digit.
Invalid or unreadable configured files stop startup.
.Pp
Valid previous assignments are retained, then remaining services receive the
lowest permitted free external port at or above 1024 in service-name order,
separately for TCP and UDP.
Saved assignments never authorize an allocation.
Insufficient ports reject the whole candidate, not just individual services.
.Pp
The complete
.Dq mape
anchor is validated and loaded with generated
.Cm pass in quick
redirects to the loopback targets.
The administrator must position the parent anchor, manage source tables,
and remove competing manual rules.
Earlier
.Cm block quick
rules can prevent matching.
No parent ruleset is modified and
.Xr pf 4
is never disabled.
Unchanged healthy renewals avoid reloading
.Xr pf 4 .
Lease withdrawal or expiry removes the owned rules.
Publishing does not reserve ports against outbound NAT, check listeners,
or prove ISP reachability.
.Sh STATUS AND HISTORY
.Nm
atomically publishes
.Pa status.json
in
.Va MAPED_STATE_DIR
.Pq default Pa /var/db/maped
on each reconciliation cycle and during application and withdrawal.
The file uses base Perl's
.Li JSON::PP
and requires no additional packages.
It is readable only by
.Li root
and is not used to authorize service or establish ownership.
.Pp
Schema version 1 includes a UTC
.Cm last-update
field, current status, live confirmation and estimated expiry timestamps,
the applied IPv4 address, CE and BR IPv6 addresses, delegated prefix,
and all inclusive TCP/UDP port ranges.
Only active or temporarily degraded service advertises an allocation.
Consumers must check freshness: a stopped daemon or failed write can leave an
old file behind, including after a one-shot invocation.
.Pp
The persistent
.Cm record
array records successfully applied allocation changes, including PSID-only
changes, with UTC
.Cm first-seen
and
.Cm last-seen
observation dates.
Unchanged healthy observations update the last record instead of appending.
History survives restart and withdrawal, is bounded only when
.Va MAPED_MAX_HISTORY
is set, and cannot reconstruct changes while the daemon was stopped.
These dates are observations, not exact ISP assignment times.
Invalid history stops startup rather than silently discarding records.
.Pp
The
.Cm published_endpoints
array lists successfully applied inbound services and their external address
and port, protocol, loopback target, and optional source table.
It is empty outside active or temporarily degraded service.
The persistent
.Cm publish_events
array records endpoint changes with UTC
.Cm at
timestamps, reporting status, and the complete endpoint list.
An empty endpoint list records withdrawal or loss of confirmed configuration;
a failed cleanup does not prove kernel removal.
Neither in-progress nor failed candidates are advertised.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/local/libexec/maped/maped-publish -compact
.It Pa /etc/maped.conf
Default
.Nm
configuration file.
.It Pa /etc/pf.anchors/mape
Default generated
.Xr pf 4
anchor file.
.It Pa /etc/rc.d/maped
.Xr rc.d 8
control script.
.It Pa /usr/local/libexec/maped/maped-derive
MAP-E parameter derivation helper.
.It Pa /usr/local/libexec/maped/maped-down
Runtime teardown helper.
.It Pa /usr/local/libexec/maped/maped-publish
Internal validated-candidate
.Xr pf 4
rule renderer.
.It Pa /usr/local/libexec/maped/maped-up
Runtime configuration helper.
.It Pa /usr/local/sbin/maped
Daemon executable.
.It Pa /var/db/maped/applied.conf
Recorded ownership state for active resources.
.It Pa /var/db/maped/lease.state
Default lease state cache.
.It Pa /var/db/maped/status.json
Atomic JSON status and persistent allocation history (mode 0600).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std maped
.Sh SEE ALSO
